<title>PORTUGAL: World copper production grows in January - ICSG.</title>
<headline>World copper production grows in January - ICSG.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>World copper production and consumption both grew strongly in January while the overall market remained in surplus, according to the International Copper Study Group's (ICSG) April bulletin.</p>
<p>Mine output was up 12.4 percent compared with January last year and primary refined production increased by 8.2 percent.</p>
<p>Consumption of refined copper grew a year-on-year 12 percent, helped by particularly strong demand in the United States and China.</p>
<p>The ICSG said the average London Metal Exchange (LME) spot price for January was $2,434 per tonne and $2,405 in February.</p>
<p>The following figures are expressed in thousand tonnes unless stated otherwise:</p>
<p>				    Jan 1997     Dec 1996   Jan 1996</p>
<p>World consumption		  1,074	    983	  959</p>
<p>World mine capacity		1,076	  1,070	1,017</p>
<p>World mine production		941	    939	  837</p>
<p>Percent capacity</p>
<p>utilisation			   87.5	   87.5	 87.5</p>
<p>Primary refined production	 937	    934	  866</p>
<p>Secondary refined production     170	    145	  157</p>
<p>Total refined production	 1,107	  1,079	1,022</p>
<p>Percent scrap in total</p>
<p>refined production		  15.3	   13.4	 15.3</p>
<p>Refined stocks</p>
<p>end of period			  531	    478	  747</p>
<p>Refined surplus			 33	     96	   63</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +351-1 3538254</p>
